.TH RANDOMWIRE 1 "November 2026" "randomwire 0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
randomwire \- screen end-fed random wire antenna lengths
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B randomwire
.RB [ --test ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Interactive ncurses utility that excludes lengths near half-wave multiples across selected amateur bands and ranks remaining intervals by worst-band resonance clearance. Lengths are entered in feet; results include meters.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --test
Run numerical regression tests and exit; returns nonzero on failure.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Up, Down, Space
Move and toggle band selection.
.TP
.B A, N
Select all or none.
.TP
.B C, W
Calculate candidates or analyze an existing wire.
.TP
.B M, S
Toggle quarter-wave minimum or edit settings.
.TP
.B Q
Quit or return from results. Enter also returns from results.
.SH LIMITATIONS
The default 5 percent exclusion margin is a heuristic. This program does not predict impedance, SWR, tuner compatibility or efficiency. The 60 meter envelope is not a transmit authorization. Verify the installed antenna with an analyzer. Settings are not persistent.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on normal exit or passing tests; 1 on regression failure; 2 on invalid arguments.
